BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Tremorlog) Tj T* () Tj T* (EXECUTIVE SUMMARY) Tj T* () Tj T* (Tremorlog, a student startup from our university) Tj T* () Tj T* (The Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Parkinson's disease is a progressive neurological disorder which effects close to one million) Tj T* (people in the United States, and tremor is one of the most visible and disruptive symptoms. The) Tj T* (problem is that the way doctors currently track it is very outdated. A patient with Parkinson's) Tj T* (typically sees their neurologist every three to six months, and the appointment is short.) Tj T* (During that time the doctor observes the patient, asks questions, and makes a judgement about) Tj T* (how medication is working. But Parkinson's symptoms fluctuate alot during the day and from week) Tj T* (to week, depending on medication timing, sleep, stress and many other factors. So what the) Tj T* (neurologist sees in the room is only a snapshot, and often not a representative one. Patients) Tj T* (are asked to remember how they did over the past months, and memory is unreliable especially) Tj T* (when the disease can also effect cognition. Some patients keep paper diaries but these are) Tj T* (inconsistent and subjective. As a result medication decisions are sometimes made with) Tj T* (incomplete information, and worsening symptoms may go unnoticed for months. There is a real gap) Tj T* (in remote monitoring of movement disorders, unlike conditions such as diabetes where home) Tj T* (devices provide continuous data.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Tremorlog is a web application that fills this gap in a simple way. The patient, or a) Tj T* (caregiver, opens the app on a phone, tablet or laptop and records a short video, around thirty) Tj T* (seconds, of their hands at rest and holding a posture, following simple on screen prompts. This) Tj T* (takes about two minutes and is meant to be done once a day at a consistent time. Our software) Tj T* (then processes the video using computer vision to estimate tremor amplitude and frequency and) Tj T* (generates a daily score. Over time the app builds a trend line which the patient can see too.) Tj T* (On the other side, the neurologist has a clinician dashboard that shows each patient's trend,) Tj T* (flags significant changes, and lets them review the actual video clips if they want to. Before) Tj T* (an appointment the doctor can see weeks of data rather than relying on a single observation. We) Tj T* (think this makes visits more productive and could allow earlier adjustments to treatment. We) Tj T* (chose a web app rather than a native mobile app so that there is nothing to download, which) Tj T* (matters because many Parkinson's patients are older and not always comfortable with technology.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (There are approximately one million people living with Parkinson's in the US and about sixty) Tj T* (thousand new diagnoses each year. Beyond Parkinson's the same approach could extend to) Tj T* (essential tremor and other movement disorders which would make the market several times bigger.) Tj T* (There are also roughly several thousand practicing neurologists and movement disorder) Tj T* (specialists. The remote patient monitoring market is growing quickly, driven by changes in how) Tj T* (telehealth is reimbursed and by greater acceptance from both patients and clinicians after the) Tj T* (pandemic. We have not yet done a full bottom up market sizing but if even a small percentage of) Tj T* (Parkinson's patients were paying a monthly fee through their clinic this would be a meaningful) Tj T* (business. Our initial target is small and mid sized neurology practices and movement disorder) Tj T* (clinics because they can make purchasing decisions faster than large hospital systems.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our plan is to sell subscriptions to clinics, not to individual patients. The clinic pays a) Tj T* (monthly fee per active patient enrolled, which we are currently testing at a price in the range) Tj T* (of fifteen to twenty five dollars per patient per month. This is partly justified because) Tj T* (remote monitoring services may be billable by clinics under existing reimbursement codes,) Tj T* (although we have not yet confirmed exactly which codes apply to our product and this is) Tj T* (something we need to research with a healthcare reimbursement expert. Secondary revenue could) Tj T* (come later from anonymized data partnerships with pharmaceutical companies running clinical) Tj ET
endstream
