BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (trials who need objective symptom measures, but this raises privacy questions which we will) Tj T* (address carefully and only with patient consent. Our costs are mainly cloud hosting and video) Tj T* (storage, which are significant because video files are large, plus development time.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (There are other players in this space. Some companies have wearable sensors that measure) Tj T* (tremor, and one or two larger companies have FDA cleared devices worn on the wrist. These are) Tj T* (more clinically validated than we are, but they require buying and shipping hardware, are) Tj T* (expensive and patients must wear them. There are also general telehealth platforms which allow) Tj T* (video visits but do not give continuous or quantitative data. Finally there are symptom diary) Tj T* (apps which are cheap but rely on self reporting. Our advantage is that we need no special) Tj T* (hardware, only a camera that the patient already owns, and so our cost to deploy is very low.) Tj T* (Our weakness is that video based measurement is probably less accurate than a dedicated sensor,) Tj T* (and we have not yet formally validated our scores against clinical rating scales. We know this) Tj T* (is the biggest question mark about our product.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Priyanka Venkataraman leads product and clinical relationships. She is a senior studying) Tj T* (neuroscience and has volunteered at a movement disorders clinic, where the idea started after) Tj T* (she saw how little information doctors had between visits. Desmond Okafor-Reyes is our lead) Tj T* (engineer, studying computer science, and he built the prototype including the video analysis) Tj T* (pipeline. Callum Tishkoff handles business operations, finance and the company registration,) Tj T* (and is studying business administration. We do not currently have a physician on the team, but) Tj T* (we have been in conversation with a neurologist who has agreed to informally advise us. We) Tj T* (recognize that a clinical advisor and someone with regulatory experience are needed.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (So far we have defined the core concept, built a working prototype that handles video capture,) Tj T* (scoring and the clinician dashboard, and registered the company. Our first client, a small) Tj T* (neurology practice, has paid for a pilot covering a limited number of patients, which gave us) Tj T* (our first revenue and a lot of useful feedback. The legal entity itself is still not fully) Tj T* (formed, and we need to sort out the formal structure and ownership split between founders.) Tj T* (Revenue to date is very small, only the pilot fee, and costs have been mostly covered by the) Tj T* (founders personally plus small savings. We project that with ten clinics and around two hundred) Tj T* (patients we could reach approximately fifty thousand dollars in annual recurring revenue,) Tj T* (though this depends on assumptions about pricing and adoption that we have not tested widely.) Tj T* (We also do not yet have a website.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Are Asking For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are asking for prize funding to support three things. First, to run a validation study) Tj T* (comparing our tremor scores with standard clinical ratings, ideally with the help of a) Tj T* (university medical partner. Second, to get legal advice on forming the company properly and on) Tj T* (privacy and health data rules including what compliance is needed for handling patient video.) Tj T* (Third, to build a basic website and expand the pilot to several more clinics. Beyond money we) Tj T* (would value mentorship from people with healthcare startup experience, introductions to) Tj T* (neurologists, and guidance on the regulatory pathway. We believe Tremorlog addresses a real and) Tj T* (underserved need and we are committed to working on it after graduation.) Tj ET
endstream
